  She reads the Hotel — the backward letters in the window that the lake below would reflect as their true names. She reads the warm air. She reads the brick at the threshold, which is different from the brick
  on the road — worn differently, held differently, the threshold knowing it is a threshold.

  She writes one more line, for the novice who comes after:

  The door does not need to be forced. It has been explaining itself this whole time. You were listening. That was the fare.

  She closes the document.

  She looks at the Judge.

  She walks through the door.

